  "deployment": "Wall brain updated (six files), service restarted by systemd, original Off mode kept. A black panel check ran on the real wall: display_mode went to frame and back to off, and a pictures check followed by /services on one kept-alive connection both answered. Final signed app installed on the iPhone 18 Pro Max.",
  "review": "Independent review of every unit with a skeptic pass, two fix rounds with a reviewer each, a test writer for the shared display plumbing, and a visual critic pass over every screenshot followed by a visual fix round.",
  "limitations": [
    "Physical review is the owner's: touch on the phone, reading the guest QR off the real LEDs with a camera, and the calibration photo on the real panel.",
    "Static captures use a fixture wall with no display session, so their wall frames show the fixture artwork. Live captures (panel running, guest code showing, at 64 and 192) show the true wall frame.",
    "The 64 wall now refuses guest codes that would need modules smaller than 2 LEDs, as the shipped version before this batch did. Long network names or passwords need a 192 wall."
  ],
  "tracking_semantics": "IDs indicate finished implementation; roadmap checkboxes await physical review."
